[h1]Spire Mentor: beta[/h1]

[b]Beta build of Spire Mentor, for testing.[/b] Unsubscribe from the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3821016481]regular Spire Mentor item[/url] while this one is installed: the game loads only one mod per id. Everything the regular item does, this one does too; its page has the full description, keys and settings.

[h2]New in this beta (0.10.6-beta.1)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]A steadier badge[/b]: the advisor's quick thinks after each action no longer flash "thinking ●○○" on the Spire Mentor badge, which made the badge and the [b]⛶ Exit fullscreen[/b] button beside it jump. "thinking" shows only when a think takes longer than about half a second.
[*][b]Aiming at an enemy[/b]: with the cursor on an enemy, the targeting arrow sometimes stayed gray (no target) until you moved around. Now the enemy under the cursor always takes the aim. If you still see a gray arrow on an enemy, please send a bug report (Ctrl+Shift+B): the log now says what was in the way.
[/list]
Everything else is the regular item's 0.10.5.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Windows only.[/b] The AI runs as a bundled Windows program (SimAdvisor.exe). On Mac or Linux the mod loads but the coach cannot start.
[*][b]Game builds v0.107.1 (stable) and v0.111.0 (public beta).[/b] A game update can break the mod until a new version is out.
[*][b]BaseLib[/b] (by Alchyr), which Steam installs alongside this mod as a required item.
[/list]

[h2]Reporting a bug[/h2]
Press [b]Ctrl+Shift+B[/b] (or [b]Panels → Report a bug[/b]) the moment something goes wrong, say what happened in one line, and press [b]Send report[/b]. Nothing is sent until you press Send. Paste the link it puts on your clipboard into a comment here or a GitHub issue.

